IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P7-gates`

-- P7-sandboxes: Chapter VI, Articles 57 to 59 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by
-- Regulation (EU) 2026/1744): AI regulatory sandboxes, the detailed arrangements for them, and the further processing of personal data in them.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone. Every function takes `the date asked` first (the version in force and the date of
-- application come from the keel through P7-gates). A result of NOTHING is "not covered"; JUST FALSE is the text's own no.
-- Group `General`: Chapter VI applies from 2 August 2026 (Art 113 second paragraph), so before that date every function answers NOTHING.
-- The as-enacted text of a passage the Omnibus replaced is in its own function (quoted from the base file); the dispatcher dispatches on the version.
-- The text is the Publications Office consolidation of 27.7.2026, a rendering with no legal effect.

DECLARE `Art 57 party` IS ONE OF
    `Art 57 Member State`
    `Art 57 national competent authority`

DECLARE `Art 57 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 57(1) have a national AI regulatory sandbox operational`
    `Art 57(11) inform the AI Office of the decision to suspend the testing or the participation`
    `Art 57(16) submit the annual report to the AI Office and to the Board`
    `Art 58(2)(a) inform the applicant of the decision on the application`

§ `Article 57(1): at least one national AI regulatory sandbox, operational by a date`

-- src:848 | 1. Member States shall ensure that their competent authorities establish at least one AI regulatory sandbox at national level, which shall be operational by 2 August 2027. That sandbox may also be established jointly with the competent authorities of other Member States. The Commission may provide technical support, advice and tools for the establishment and operation of AI regulatory sandboxes.
@ref Art 57(1) first subparagraph as amended: the date (src:848)
`Art 57(1) as amended the date by which a national AI regulatory sandbox must be operational` MEANS Date 2 8 2027

-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1401 | 1. Member States shall ensure that their competent authorities establish at least one AI regulatory sandbox at national level, which shall be operational by 2 August 2026. That sandbox may also be established jointly with the competent authorities of other Member States. The Commission may provide technical support, advice and tools for the establishment and operation of AI regulatory sandboxes.
@ref Art 57(1) first subparagraph as enacted: the date (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1401)
`Art 57(1) as enacted the date by which a national AI regulatory sandbox must be operational` MEANS Date 2 8 2026

-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1401 | 1. Member States shall ensure that their competent authorities establish at least one AI regulatory sandbox at national level, which shall be operational by 2 August 2026. That sandbox may also be established jointly with the competent authorities of other Member States. The Commission may provide technical support, advice and tools for the establishment and operation of AI regulatory sandboxes.
@ref Art 57(1) first subparagraph first sentence as enacted (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1401)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `a national AI regulatory sandbox established by the competent authorities is operational` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the obligation is fulfilled by participation in an existing sandbox under the second subparagraph` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 57(1) as enacted the Member State has ensured that a national AI regulatory sandbox is operational` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a national AI regulatory sandbox established by the competent authorities is operational` OR `the obligation is fulfilled by participation in an existing sandbox under the second subparagraph` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the date asked` AT MOST `Art 57(1) as enacted the date by which a national AI regulatory sandbox must be operational` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by" the date: the day on which the sandbox "shall be operational" has not yet passed
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "which shall be operational by 2 August 2026"

-- src:848 | 1. Member States shall ensure that their competent authorities establish at least one AI regulatory sandbox at national level, which shall be operational by 2 August 2027. That sandbox may also be established jointly with the competent authorities of other Member States. The Commission may provide technical support, advice and tools for the establishment and operation of AI regulatory sandboxes.
@ref Art 57(1) first subparagraph first sentence as amended (src:848)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `a national AI regulatory sandbox established by the competent authorities is operational` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the obligation is fulfilled by participation in an existing sandbox under the second subparagraph` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 57(1) as amended the Member State has ensured that a national AI regulatory sandbox is operational` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a national AI regulatory sandbox established by the competent authorities is operational` OR `the obligation is fulfilled by participation in an existing sandbox under the second subparagraph` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the date asked` AT MOST `Art 57(1) as amended the date by which a national AI regulatory sandbox must be operational` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by" the date: the day on which the sandbox "shall be operational" has not yet passed
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "which shall be operational by 2 August 2027"

@ref Art 57(1) first subparagraph first sentence (dispatcher: gate, then the version in force; src:848)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `a national AI regulatory sandbox established by the competent authorities is operational` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the obligation is fulfilled by participation in an existing sandbox under the second subparagraph` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 57(1) the Member State has ensured that a national AI regulatory sandbox is operational` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
         WHEN `as enacted` THEN `Art 57(1) as enacted the Member State has ensured that a national AI regulatory sandbox is operational` `the date asked` `a national AI regulatory sandbox established by the competent authorities is operational` `the obligation is fulfilled by participation in an existing sandbox under the second subparagraph`  -- VERSION as enacted
         WHEN `as amended` THEN `Art 57(1) as amended the Member State has ensured that a national AI regulatory sandbox is operational` `the date asked` `a national AI regulatory sandbox established by the competent authorities is operational` `the obligation is fulfilled by participation in an existing sandbox under the second subparagraph`  -- VERSION as amended

-- The clock of a trace of the Member State's duty is a day number: it starts on the day Chapter VI applies (Art 113 second paragraph),
-- and the duty is to have the sandbox operational by the date the version in force gives.

-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1401 | 1. Member States shall ensure that their competent authorities establish at least one AI regulatory sandbox at national level, which shall be operational by 2 August 2026. That sandbox may also be established jointly with the competent authorities of other Member States. The Commission may provide technical support, advice and tools for the establishment and operation of AI regulatory sandboxes.
@ref Art 57(1) first subparagraph first sentence as enacted (the duty and its deadline) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1401)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 57 party` `Art 57 act`
`Art 57(1) as enacted the Member State's duty to have a national AI regulatory sandbox operational` MEANS
    PARTY `Art 57 Member State`
    MUST `Art 57(1) have a national AI regulatory sandbox operational`
    WITHIN (Day `Art 57(1) as enacted the date by which a national AI regulatory sandbox must be operational`) MINUS (Day `Art 113 second paragraph the general date of application`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `Art 57 Member State` BECAUSE "no national AI regulatory sandbox was operational by the date Article 57(1) gives"

-- src:848 | 1. Member States shall ensure that their competent authorities establish at least one AI regulatory sandbox at national level, which shall be operational by 2 August 2027. That sandbox may also be established jointly with the competent authorities of other Member States. The Commission may provide technical support, advice and tools for the establishment and operation of AI regulatory sandboxes.
@ref Art 57(1) first subparagraph first sentence as amended (the duty and its deadline) (src:848)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 57 party` `Art 57 act`
`Art 57(1) as amended the Member State's duty to have a national AI regulatory sandbox operational` MEANS
    PARTY `Art 57 Member State`
    MUST `Art 57(1) have a national AI regulatory sandbox operational`
    WITHIN (Day `Art 57(1) as amended the date by which a national AI regulatory sandbox must be operational`) MINUS (Day `Art 113 second paragraph the general date of application`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `Art 57 Member State` BECAUSE "no national AI regulatory sandbox was operational by the date Article 57(1) gives"

@ref Art 57(1) first subparagraph first sentence (the duty: gate, then the version in force; src:848)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 57 party` `Art 57 act`
`Art 57(1) the Member State's duty to have a national AI regulatory sandbox operational` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: Chapter VI does not apply on the date asked
    ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
         WHEN `as enacted` THEN `Art 57(1) as enacted the Member State's duty to have a national AI regulatory sandbox operational`  -- VERSION as enacted
         WHEN `as amended` THEN `Art 57(1) as amended the Member State's duty to have a national AI regulatory sandbox operational`  -- VERSION as amended

-- src:848 | 1. Member States shall ensure that their competent authorities establish at least one AI regulatory sandbox at national level, which shall be operational by 2 August 2027. That sandbox may also be established jointly with the competent authorities of other Member States. The Commission may provide technical support, advice and tools for the establishment and operation of AI regulatory sandboxes.
@ref Art 57(1) first subparagraph last sentence (src:848)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the support is technical support, advice or tools for the establishment and operation of AI regulatory sandboxes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 57(1) the Commission may provide technical support, advice and tools` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        IF `the support is technical support, advice or tools for the establishment and operation of AI regulatory sandboxes` THEN JUST TRUE  -- the grant: "The Commission may provide technical support, advice and tools for the establishment and operation of AI regulatory sandboxes"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names technical support, advice and tools and says nothing of other help

§ `Article 57(1) second subparagraph and Article 57(2)`

-- src:850 | The obligation under the first subparagraph may also be fulfilled by participating in an existing sandbox in so far as that participation provides an equivalent level of national coverage for the participating Member States.
@ref Art 57(1) second subparagraph (src:850)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Member State participates in an existing sandbox` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that participation provides an equivalent level of national coverage for the participating Member States` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 57(1) second subparagraph the obligation is fulfilled by participation in an existing sandbox` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        IF `the Member State participates in an existing sandbox` AND `that participation provides an equivalent level of national coverage for the participating Member States` THEN JUST TRUE  -- the grant: "may also be fulfilled by participating in an existing sandbox in so far as that participation provides an equivalent level of national coverage"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in so far as that participation provides an equivalent level of national coverage"

-- src:851 | 2. Additional AI regulatory sandboxes at regional or local level, or established jointly with the competent authorities of other Member States may also be established.
@ref Art 57(2) (src:851)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the sandbox is at regional or local level` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sandbox is established jointly with the competent authorities of other Member States` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 57(2) an additional AI regulatory sandbox may be established` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        IF `the sandbox is at regional or local level` OR `the sandbox is established jointly with the competent authorities of other Member States` THEN JUST TRUE  -- the grant: "Additional AI regulatory sandboxes at regional or local level, or established jointly with the competent authorities of other Member States may also be established"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names regional or local level and joint establishment; it does not say that no other additional sandbox may be established

§ `Article 57(3) and (3a): the European Data Protection Supervisor and the AI Office`

