         WHEN `as enacted` THEN `Art 57(10) as enacted the national competent authorities have associated the other authorities with the sandbox` `the innovative AI systems involve the processing of personal data` `the innovative AI systems otherwise fall under the supervisory remit of other authorities` `the data protection authorities and the other authorities are associated with the operation` `they are involved in the supervision of those aspects`  -- VERSION as enacted
         WHEN `as amended` THEN `Art 57(10) as amended the national competent authorities have associated the other authorities with the sandbox` `the innovative AI systems involve the processing of personal data` `the innovative AI systems otherwise fall under the supervisory remit of other authorities` `the data protection authorities and the other authorities are associated with the operation` `they are involved in the supervision of those aspects`  -- VERSION as amended

-- src:875 | 11. The AI regulatory sandboxes shall not affect the supervisory or corrective powers of the competent authorities supervising the sandboxes, including at regional or local level. Any significant risks to health and safety and fundamental rights identified during the development and testing of such AI systems shall result in an adequate mitigation. National competent authorities shall have the power to temporarily or permanently suspend the testing process, or the participation in the sandbox if no effective mitigation is possible, and shall inform the AI Office of such decision. National competent authorities shall exercise their supervisory powers within the limits of the relevant law, using their discretionary powers when implementing legal provisions in respect of a specific AI regulatory sandbox project, with the objective of supporting innovation in AI in the Union.
@ref Art 57(11) first sentence (src:875)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the powers are those of the competent authorities supervising the sandboxes, including at regional or local level` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 57(11) the sandboxes affect the supervisory or corrective powers of the competent authorities` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        IF `the powers are those of the competent authorities supervising the sandboxes, including at regional or local level` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The AI regulatory sandboxes shall not affect the supervisory or corrective powers of the competent authorities supervising the sandboxes"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the provision speaks only of the case it names

-- src:875 | 11. The AI regulatory sandboxes shall not affect the supervisory or corrective powers of the competent authorities supervising the sandboxes, including at regional or local level. Any significant risks to health and safety and fundamental rights identified during the development and testing of such AI systems shall result in an adequate mitigation. National competent authorities shall have the power to temporarily or permanently suspend the testing process, or the participation in the sandbox if no effective mitigation is possible, and shall inform the AI Office of such decision. National competent authorities shall exercise their supervisory powers within the limits of the relevant law, using their discretionary powers when implementing legal provisions in respect of a specific AI regulatory sandbox project, with the objective of supporting innovation in AI in the Union.
@ref Art 57(11) second sentence (src:875)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `significant risks to health and safety or fundamental rights were identified during the development and testing of the AI systems` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the significant risks resulted in an adequate mitigation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 57(11) significant risks have resulted in an adequate mitigation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT (`significant risks to health and safety or fundamental rights were identified during the development and testing of the AI systems`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any significant risks to health and safety and fundamental rights identified during the development and testing of such AI systems"
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the significant risks resulted in an adequate mitigation`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any significant risks to health and safety and fundamental rights identified during the development and testing of such AI systems shall result in an adequate mitigation"

-- src:875 | 11. The AI regulatory sandboxes shall not affect the supervisory or corrective powers of the competent authorities supervising the sandboxes, including at regional or local level. Any significant risks to health and safety and fundamental rights identified during the development and testing of such AI systems shall result in an adequate mitigation. National competent authorities shall have the power to temporarily or permanently suspend the testing process, or the participation in the sandbox if no effective mitigation is possible, and shall inform the AI Office of such decision. National competent authorities shall exercise their supervisory powers within the limits of the relevant law, using their discretionary powers when implementing legal provisions in respect of a specific AI regulatory sandbox project, with the objective of supporting innovation in AI in the Union.
@ref Art 57(11) third sentence (the power) (src:875)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `no effective mitigation is possible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the national competent authority suspends the testing process, or the participation in the sandbox, temporarily or permanently` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 57(11) the national competent authority has the power to suspend the testing process or the participation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT (`no effective mitigation is possible`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if no effective mitigation is possible"
        IF `the national competent authority suspends the testing process, or the participation in the sandbox, temporarily or permanently` THEN JUST TRUE  -- the grant: "National competent authorities shall have the power to temporarily or permanently suspend the testing process, or the participation in the sandbox if no effective mitigation is possible"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is for suspending the testing process or the participation

-- src:875 | 11. The AI regulatory sandboxes shall not affect the supervisory or corrective powers of the competent authorities supervising the sandboxes, including at regional or local level. Any significant risks to health and safety and fundamental rights identified during the development and testing of such AI systems shall result in an adequate mitigation. National competent authorities shall have the power to temporarily or permanently suspend the testing process, or the participation in the sandbox if no effective mitigation is possible, and shall inform the AI Office of such decision. National competent authorities shall exercise their supervisory powers within the limits of the relevant law, using their discretionary powers when implementing legal provisions in respect of a specific AI regulatory sandbox project, with the objective of supporting innovation in AI in the Union.
@ref Art 57(11) third sentence (informing the AI Office) (src:875)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the national competent authority decided to suspend the testing process or the participation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the national competent authority informs the AI Office of the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 57(11) the national competent authority has informed the AI Office of its decision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT (`the national competent authority decided to suspend the testing process or the participation`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such decision"
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the national competent authority informs the AI Office of the decision`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall inform the AI Office of such decision"

-- src:875 | 11. The AI regulatory sandboxes shall not affect the supervisory or corrective powers of the competent authorities supervising the sandboxes, including at regional or local level. Any significant risks to health and safety and fundamental rights identified during the development and testing of such AI systems shall result in an adequate mitigation. National competent authorities shall have the power to temporarily or permanently suspend the testing process, or the participation in the sandbox if no effective mitigation is possible, and shall inform the AI Office of such decision. National competent authorities shall exercise their supervisory powers within the limits of the relevant law, using their discretionary powers when implementing legal provisions in respect of a specific AI regulatory sandbox project, with the objective of supporting innovation in AI in the Union.
@ref Art 57(11) fourth sentence (src:875)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the national competent authorities exercise their supervisory powers within the limits of the relevant law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they use their discretionary powers when implementing legal provisions in respect of a specific sandbox project with the objective of supporting innovation in AI in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 57(11) the national competent authorities have exercised their supervisory powers within the limits of the relevant law` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the national competent authorities exercise their supervisory powers within the limits of the relevant law` AND `they use their discretionary powers when implementing legal provisions in respect of a specific sandbox project with the objective of supporting innovation in AI in the Union`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "National competent authorities shall exercise their supervisory powers within the limits of the relevant law, using their discretionary powers when implementing legal provisions in respect of a specific AI regulatory sandbox project, with the objective of supporting innovation in AI in the Union"

-- Art 57(11) third sentence: the decision to inform the AI Office has no time limit and no stated consequence (no breach path)
@ref Art 57(11) third sentence (informing the AI Office; src:875)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 57 party` `Art 57 act`
`Art 57(11) the national competent authority's duty to inform the AI Office of its decision to suspend` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: Chapter VI does not apply on the date asked
    ELSE
        PARTY `Art 57 national competent authority`
        MUST `Art 57(11) inform the AI Office of the decision to suspend the testing or the participation`
        HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:876 | 12. Providers and prospective providers participating in the AI regulatory sandbox shall remain liable under applicable Union and national liability law for any damage inflicted on third parties as a result of the experimentation taking place in the sandbox. However, provided that the prospective providers observe the specific plan and the terms and conditions for their participation and follow in good faith the guidance given by the national competent authority, no administrative fines shall be imposed by the authorities for infringements of this Regulation. Where other competent authorities responsible for other Union and national law were actively involved in the supervision of the AI system in the sandbox and provided guidance for compliance, no administrative fines shall be imposed regarding that law.
@ref Art 57(12) first sentence (src:876)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `damage was inflicted on third parties as a result of the experimentation taking place in the sandbox` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 57(12) the provider remains liable under applicable Union and national liability law for damage inflicted on third parties` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT (`Art 57 Article 2(2) leaves the provision to apply` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 57 "" 12) THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" (S14: the keel's `Art 2(2)` answered JUST FALSE)
        IF `damage was inflicted on third parties as a result of the experimentation taking place in the sandbox` THEN JUST TRUE  -- the grant: "Providers and prospective providers participating in the AI regulatory sandbox shall remain liable under applicable Union and national liability law for any damage inflicted on third parties as a result of the experimentation taking place in the sandbox"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): without damage to third parties from the experimentation the sentence says nothing

-- src:876 | 12. Providers and prospective providers participating in the AI regulatory sandbox shall remain liable under applicable Union and national liability law for any damage inflicted on third parties as a result of the experimentation taking place in the sandbox. However, provided that the prospective providers observe the specific plan and the terms and conditions for their participation and follow in good faith the guidance given by the national competent authority, no administrative fines shall be imposed by the authorities for infringements of this Regulation. Where other competent authorities responsible for other Union and national law were actively involved in the supervision of the AI system in the sandbox and provided guidance for compliance, no administrative fines shall be imposed regarding that law.
