        IF NOT (`Art 57 Article 2(2) leaves the provision to apply` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 57 "" 12) THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" (S14: the keel's `Art 2(2)` answered JUST FALSE)
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the prospective provider observes the specific plan and the terms and conditions for their participation` AND `the prospective provider follows in good faith the guidance given by the national competent authority`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provided that the prospective providers observe the specific plan and the terms and conditions for their participation and follow in good faith the guidance given by the national competent authority, no administrative fines shall be imposed by the authorities for infringements of this Regulation"

