        OTHERWISE JUST (`the Commission adopts implementing acts specifying the detailed arrangements for the establishment, development, implementation, operation, governance, and supervision of the AI regulatory sandboxes`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Commission shall adopt implementing acts specifying the detailed arrangements for the establishment, development, implementation, operation, governance, and supervision of the AI regulatory sandboxes"

@ref Art 58(1) lead (dispatcher: gate, then the version in force; src:887)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Commission adopts implementing acts specifying the detailed arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 58(1) the Commission has adopted the implementing acts specifying the detailed arrangements` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
         WHEN `as enacted` THEN `Art 58(1) as enacted the Commission has adopted the implementing acts specifying the detailed arrangements` `the Commission adopts implementing acts specifying the detailed arrangements`  -- VERSION as enacted
         WHEN `as amended` THEN `Art 58(1) as amended the Commission has adopted the implementing acts specifying the detailed arrangements` `the Commission adopts implementing acts specifying the detailed arrangements`  -- VERSION as amended

