        IF NOT (`the provider is an SME, including a start-up`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "free of charge for SMEs, including start-ups"
        OTHERWISE JUST (`no fee is charged for access to the sandbox` OR `the national competent authority recovers exceptional costs in a fair and proportionate manner`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that access to the AI regulatory sandboxes is free of charge for SMEs, including start-ups, without prejudice to exceptional costs that national competent authorities may recover in a fair and proportionate manner"

