§ `Article 59: further processing of personal data for developing certain AI systems in the public interest in the sandbox`

-- src:911 | (a) AI systems shall be developed for safeguarding substantial public interest by a public authority or another natural or legal person and in one or more of the following areas:
-- src:912 | (i) public safety and public health, including disease detection, diagnosis prevention, control and treatment and improvement of health care systems;
-- src:913 | (ii) a high level of protection and improvement of the quality of the environment, protection of biodiversity, protection against pollution, green transition measures, climate change mitigation and adaptation measures;
-- src:914 | (iii) energy sustainability;
-- src:915 | (iv) safety and resilience of transport systems and mobility, critical infrastructure and networks;
-- src:916 | (v) efficiency and quality of public administration and public services;
@ref Art 59(1)(a)(i) to (v) (the areas) (src:911-916)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`Art 59(1)(a) the areas of substantial public interest` MEANS
    LIST
        "public safety and public health, including disease detection, diagnosis prevention, control and treatment and improvement of health care systems"
      , "a high level of protection and improvement of the quality of the environment, protection of biodiversity, protection against pollution, green transition measures, climate change mitigation and adaptation measures"
      , "energy sustainability"
      , "safety and resilience of transport systems and mobility, critical infrastructure and networks"
      , "efficiency and quality of public administration and public services"

@ref Art 59(1)(a) (the area is one of the areas; src:911-916)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the area` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 59(1)(a) the area is one of the areas of substantial public interest` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        IF elem `the area` `Art 59(1)(a) the areas of substantial public interest` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "in one or more of the following areas" names areas and does not say that a system in another area is excluded; the closing is in the condition function, which reads the five areas as an alternative

-- src:911 | (a) AI systems shall be developed for safeguarding substantial public interest by a public authority or another natural or legal person and in one or more of the following areas:
-- src:912 | (i) public safety and public health, including disease detection, diagnosis prevention, control and treatment and improvement of health care systems;
-- src:913 | (ii) a high level of protection and improvement of the quality of the environment, protection of biodiversity, protection against pollution, green transition measures, climate change mitigation and adaptation measures;
-- src:914 | (iii) energy sustainability;
-- src:915 | (iv) safety and resilience of transport systems and mobility, critical infrastructure and networks;
-- src:916 | (v) efficiency and quality of public administration and public services;
@ref Art 59(1)(a) and (i) to (v) (the condition) (src:911-916)
GIVEN `the AI system is developed for safeguarding substantial public interest by a public authority or another natural or legal person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the area is public safety and public health` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the area is a high level of protection and improvement of the quality of the environment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the area is energy sustainability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the area is safety and resilience of transport systems and mobility, critical infrastructure and networks` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the area is efficiency and quality of public administration and public services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 59(1)(a) the AI system is developed for safeguarding substantial public interest in one of the areas` MEANS
        `the AI system is developed for safeguarding substantial public interest by a public authority or another natural or legal person`
    AND (   `the area is public safety and public health`
         OR `the area is a high level of protection and improvement of the quality of the environment`
         OR `the area is energy sustainability`
         OR `the area is safety and resilience of transport systems and mobility, critical infrastructure and networks`
         OR `the area is efficiency and quality of public administration and public services`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in one or more of the following areas" (the five areas are the alternatives the point closes with the list that follows)

-- src:917 | (b) the data processed are necessary for complying with one or more of the requirements referred to in Chapter III, Section 2 where those requirements cannot effectively be fulfilled by processing anonymised, synthetic or other non-personal data;
@ref Art 59(1)(b) (src:917)
GIVEN `the data processed are necessary for complying with one or more of the requirements referred to in Chapter III, Section 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those requirements cannot effectively be fulfilled by processing anonymised, synthetic or other non-personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 59(1)(b) the data processed are necessary for complying with the requirements of Chapter III, Section 2` MEANS
    `the data processed are necessary for complying with one or more of the requirements referred to in Chapter III, Section 2` AND `those requirements cannot effectively be fulfilled by processing anonymised, synthetic or other non-personal data`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the data processed are necessary for complying with one or more of the requirements referred to in Chapter III, Section 2 where those requirements cannot effectively be fulfilled by processing anonymised, synthetic or other non-personal data"

-- src:918 | (c) there are effective monitoring mechanisms to identify if any high risks to the rights and freedoms of the data subjects, as referred to in Article 35 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 and in Article 39 of Regulation (EU) 2018/1725, may arise during the sandbox experimentation, as well as response mechanisms to promptly mitigate those risks and, where necessary, stop the processing;
@ref Art 59(1)(c) (src:918)
GIVEN `there are effective monitoring mechanisms to identify if any high risks to the rights and freedoms of the data subjects, as referred to in Article 35 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 and in Article 39 of Regulation (EU) 2018/1725, may arise during the sandbox experimentation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are response mechanisms to promptly mitigate those risks and, where necessary, stop the processing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 59(1)(c) there are effective monitoring mechanisms and response mechanisms` MEANS
    `there are effective monitoring mechanisms to identify if any high risks to the rights and freedoms of the data subjects, as referred to in Article 35 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 and in Article 39 of Regulation (EU) 2018/1725, may arise during the sandbox experimentation` AND `there are response mechanisms to promptly mitigate those risks and, where necessary, stop the processing`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "there are effective monitoring mechanisms to identify if any high risks to the rights and freedoms of the data subjects ... may arise during the sandbox experimentation, as well as response mechanisms to promptly mitigate those risks and, where necessary, stop the processing"

-- src:919 | (d) any personal data to be processed in the context of the sandbox are in a functionally separate, isolated and protected data processing environment under the control of the prospective provider and only authorised persons have access to those data;
@ref Art 59(1)(d) (src:919)
GIVEN `the personal data are in a functionally separate, isolated and protected data processing environment under the control of the prospective provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `only authorised persons have access to those data` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 59(1)(d) the personal data are in a functionally separate, isolated and protected environment with access limited to authorised persons` MEANS
    `the personal data are in a functionally separate, isolated and protected data processing environment under the control of the prospective provider` AND `only authorised persons have access to those data`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any personal data to be processed in the context of the sandbox are in a functionally separate, isolated and protected data processing environment under the control of the prospective provider and only authorised persons have access to those data"

-- src:920 | (e) providers can further share the originally collected data only in accordance with Union data protection law; any personal data created in the sandbox cannot be shared outside the sandbox;
@ref Art 59(1)(e) (src:920)
GIVEN `the providers share the originally collected data further only in accordance with Union data protection law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no personal data created in the sandbox is shared outside the sandbox` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 59(1)(e) the data are shared further only in accordance with Union data protection law and no data created in the sandbox is shared outside it` MEANS
    `the providers share the originally collected data further only in accordance with Union data protection law` AND `no personal data created in the sandbox is shared outside the sandbox`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "providers can further share the originally collected data only in accordance with Union data protection law; any personal data created in the sandbox cannot be shared outside the sandbox"

-- src:921 | (f) any processing of personal data in the context of the sandbox neither leads to measures or decisions affecting the data subjects nor does it affect the application of their rights laid down in Union law on the protection of personal data;
@ref Art 59(1)(f) (src:921)
GIVEN `the processing leads to no measures or decisions affecting the data subjects` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing does not affect the application of their rights laid down in Union law on the protection of personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 59(1)(f) the processing neither leads to measures or decisions affecting the data subjects nor affects their rights` MEANS
    `the processing leads to no measures or decisions affecting the data subjects` AND `the processing does not affect the application of their rights laid down in Union law on the protection of personal data`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any processing of personal data in the context of the sandbox neither leads to measures or decisions affecting the data subjects nor does it affect the application of their rights laid down in Union law on the protection of personal data"

-- src:922 | (g) any personal data processed in the context of the sandbox are protected by means of appropriate technical and organisational measures and deleted once the participation in the sandbox has terminated or the personal data has reached the end of its retention period;
@ref Art 59(1)(g) (src:922)
GIVEN `the personal data processed are protected by means of appropriate technical and organisational measures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the personal data are deleted once the participation in the sandbox has terminated or the personal data has reached the end of its retention period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 59(1)(g) the personal data are protected by appropriate measures and deleted at the end` MEANS
    `the personal data processed are protected by means of appropriate technical and organisational measures` AND `the personal data are deleted once the participation in the sandbox has terminated or the personal data has reached the end of its retention period`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any personal data processed in the context of the sandbox are protected by means of appropriate technical and organisational measures and deleted once the participation in the sandbox has terminated or the personal data has reached the end of its retention period"

-- src:923 | (h) the logs of the processing of personal data in the context of the sandbox are kept for the duration of the participation in the sandbox, unless provided otherwise by Union or national law;
@ref Art 59(1)(h) (src:923)
GIVEN `the logs of the processing of personal data are kept for the duration of the participation in the sandbox` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Union or national law provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 59(1)(h) the logs of the processing are kept for the duration of the participation unless provided otherwise by law` MEANS
    `the logs of the processing of personal data are kept for the duration of the participation in the sandbox` OR `Union or national law provides otherwise`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the logs of the processing of personal data in the context of the sandbox are kept for the duration of the participation in the sandbox, unless provided otherwise by Union or national law"

-- src:924 | (i) a complete and detailed description of the process and rationale behind the training, testing and validation of the AI system is kept together with the testing results as part of the technical documentation referred to in Annex IV;
@ref Art 59(1)(i) (src:924)
GIVEN `a complete and detailed description of the process and rationale behind the training, testing and validation of the AI system is kept together with the testing results as part of the technical documentation referred to in Annex IV` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 59(1)(i) a complete and detailed description of the training, testing and validation is kept with the testing results` MEANS
    `a complete and detailed description of the process and rationale behind the training, testing and validation of the AI system is kept together with the testing results as part of the technical documentation referred to in Annex IV`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a complete and detailed description of the process and rationale behind the training, testing and validation of the AI system is kept together with the testing results as part of the technical documentation referred to in Annex IV"

-- src:925 | (j) a short summary of the AI project developed in the sandbox, its objectives and expected results is published on the website of the competent authorities; this obligation shall not cover sensitive operational data in relation to the activities of law enforcement, border control, immigration or asylum authorities.
@ref Art 59(1)(j) (src:925)
GIVEN `a short summary of the AI project developed in the sandbox, its objectives and expected results is published on the website of the competent authorities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the summary would disclose sensitive operational data in relation to the activities of law enforcement, border control, immigration or asylum authorities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 59(1)(j) a short summary of the AI project is published on the website of the competent authorities` MEANS
    `a short summary of the AI project developed in the sandbox, its objectives and expected results is published on the website of the competent authorities` OR `the summary would disclose sensitive operational data in relation to the activities of law enforcement, border control, immigration or asylum authorities`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a short summary of the AI project developed in the sandbox, its objectives and expected results is published on the website of the competent authorities; this obligation shall not cover sensitive operational data in relation to the activities of law enforcement, border control, immigration or asylum authorities"

-- src:910 | 1. In the AI regulatory sandbox, personal data lawfully collected for other purposes may be processed solely for the purpose of developing, training and testing certain AI systems in the sandbox when all of the following conditions are met:
@ref Art 59(1) lead (the permission, when all the conditions are met) (src:910)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the personal data were lawfully collected for other purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is solely for the purpose of developing, training and testing the AI system in the sandbox` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions of points (a) to (j) are each met` IS A LIST OF BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 59(1) the personal data may be processed in the AI regulatory sandbox for developing, training and testing the AI system` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT (`Art 57 Article 2(2) leaves the provision to apply` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 59 "" 1) THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Articles 57, 58 and 59 shall apply only in so far as the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation" (S14: the keel answered JUST FALSE)
        IF NOT (`the personal data were lawfully collected for other purposes` AND `the processing is solely for the purpose of developing, training and testing the AI system in the sandbox`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "personal data lawfully collected for other purposes may be processed solely for the purpose of developing, training and testing"
        OTHERWISE JUST (all (GIVEN c YIELD c) `the conditions of points (a) to (j) are each met`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when all of the following conditions are met" (a "may" gated by "when": split site (ii), see the fork register)

-- src:926 | 2. For the purposes of the prevention, investigation, detection or prosecution of criminal offences or the execution of criminal penalties, including safeguarding against and preventing threats to public security, under the control and responsibility of law enforcement authorities, the processing of personal data in AI regulatory sandboxes shall be based on a specific Union or national law and subject to the same cumulative conditions as referred to in paragraph 1.
@ref Art 59(2) (law enforcement purposes) (src:926)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is for the purposes of the prevention, investigation, detection or prosecution of criminal offences or the execution of criminal penalties, including safeguarding against and preventing threats to public security, under the control and responsibility of law enforcement authorities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is based on a specific Union or national law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cumulative conditions referred to in paragraph 1 are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 59(2) the processing of personal data for law enforcement purposes in the AI regulatory sandbox is lawful under this Article` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT (`Art 57 Article 2(2) leaves the provision to apply` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 59 "" 2) THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Articles 57, 58 and 59 shall apply only in so far as ..." (S14)
        IF NOT `the processing is for the purposes of the prevention, investigation, detection or prosecution of criminal offences or the execution of criminal penalties, including safeguarding against and preventing threats to public security, under the control and responsibility of law enforcement authorities` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of the prevention, investigation, detection or prosecution of criminal offences ..., under the control and responsibility of law enforcement authorities"
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the processing is based on a specific Union or national law` AND `the cumulative conditions referred to in paragraph 1 are met`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be based on a specific Union or national law and subject to the same cumulative conditions as referred to in paragraph 1"

-- src:927 | 3. Paragraph 1 is without prejudice to Union or national law which excludes processing of personal data for other purposes than those explicitly mentioned in that law, as well as to Union or national law laying down the basis for the processing of personal data which is necessary for the purpose of developing, testing or training of innovative AI systems or any other legal basis, in compliance with Union law on the protection of personal data.
@ref Art 59(3) (src:927)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the law excludes processing of personal data for other purposes than those explicitly mentioned in that law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law lays down the basis for the processing of personal data which is necessary for the purpose of developing, testing or training of innovative AI systems or any other legal basis, in compliance with Union law on the protection of personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 59(3) paragraph 1 prejudices Union or national law on the processing of personal data` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        IF `the law excludes processing of personal data for other purposes than those explicitly mentioned in that law` OR `the law lays down the basis for the processing of personal data which is necessary for the purpose of developing, testing or training of innovative AI systems or any other legal basis, in compliance with Union law on the protection of personal data` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph 1 is without prejudice to Union or national law which excludes processing of personal data for other purposes than those explicitly mentioned in that law, as well as to Union or national law laying down the basis for the processing of personal data"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the provision speaks only of the case it names
